# PLAN-2: Phase-1 kickoff — audit fair-comparison configs + build bounded proxies (CIFAR-100)

## Current evidence (Phase-0 + smoke gate PASSED)
- Phase-0 PASSED; three plumbing bugs fixed (ablation precedence, CPU dtype, GPU device placement).
- Host-GPU smoke gate PASSED (PLAN-1d): both presets EXIT 0 on cuda, no tracebacks, distinct hashes.
  full_e_hsfp counters nonzero and DIFFER from baseline (mem 4000/2000/4000; PRC 600 calls,
  mean 0.0897; reliability 551 nonuniform; dropout apply 4, active-set mean 3.75). baseline all 0.
- CIFAR-100 `model: resnet50` actually = pretrained ResNet-18 client split; edge/cloud random-init.
- Default budget: 60 global rounds, 20/200 clients/round, 10 local SSL epochs, Adam 1e-4.
- Codex sandbox has NO GPU → Claude launches GPU runs on host; Codex audits configs/artifacts.
- Provisional (INVALID) accuracy: CIFAR-100 8.10% vs SplitFL 58.4% — measured with dead ablations;
  not targets. B_d must be the strongest FAIRLY REPRODUCED baseline on the SAME partition/seed.

## Hypothesis
A fair, matched CIFAR-100 comparison harness can be established: the baselines (SplitFL, Federated,
HierFL, HSFL, HeteroSFL) and H-SFP/E-HSFP can be run on the SAME dataset partition, seed handling,
top-1 metric, and a comparable training budget. A short bounded proxy (reduced rounds) will (a)
confirm sane, increasing validation accuracy per method, (b) confirm the metric definition, and (c)
give a per-run runtime estimate to budget the full reproduction — BEFORE any full grid.

## Proposed isolated change
No algorithm change. Only: (1) a written fair-comparison audit; (2) new bounded PROXY configs
(reduced global rounds, full model/data otherwise) for a minimal method set on the SAME CIFAR-100
partition + seed; unique output dirs. Do NOT modify the real default configs.

## Invariants
- No full grid yet. Proxy budget only. Preserve uncommitted changes + all results; unique dirs.
- Fair match: same partition, seed, preprocessing/augmentation, backbone/pretraining policy, budget,
  and metric across compared methods; document any unavoidable mismatch + add a matched control.
- Do NOT weaken any baseline. No sample-level feature/gradient transfer in H-SFP. Local only.
- Respect shared ~12 GB GPU (a co-resident job uses ~4 GB) — proxies run sequentially, watch VRAM.

## Codex implementation tasks (NO GPU — audit + config prep only)
1. Record the PLAN-1d smoke-gate PASS in EXPERIMENT_REGISTRY.csv + DECISIONS.md (status=smoke-pass).
2. Fair-comparison audit for CIFAR-100 across methods {h-sfp, splitfl, federated, hierfl, hsfl,
   heterosfl}: for each, resolve dataset partition scheme + partition_hash, seed handling, top-1
   metric definition + eval protocol (which client/edge/cloud evaluated), backbone + pretraining,
   rounds/clients/local-epochs, optimizer/scheduler. Produce a matrix in a new
   `docs/optimization_loop/FAIR_COMPARISON_CIFAR100.md` and FLAG every mismatch (esp. whether all
   methods share the identical CIFAR-100 partition + seed; whether metric is top-1 acc vs other).
3. Create bounded PROXY configs (e.g. ~8–10 global rounds, otherwise full model/data, IID) for a
   MINIMAL method set: splitfl (strongest reported baseline), federated (simple sanity), h-sfp
   baseline_hsfp, and full_e_hsfp — all on the SAME CIFAR-100 partition + seed. Put them under
   `configs/proxy/` with unique output dirs. Do not touch default configs.
4. Emit, into the report, the EXACT `python main.py ...` command line for each proxy run (task,
   method, cfg, ablation if any, seed) so Claude can launch them on the host GPU.

## Tests
1. Each proxy config resolves (dry parse / `--list-configs` or a config-load unit) without error and
   yields a distinct resolved-config hash + output dir.
2. Fair-comparison matrix identifies whether partition/seed/metric are matched across methods.

## Experiment matrix
CIFAR-100; 1 dev seed; methods {splitfl, federated, h-sfp:baseline_hsfp, h-sfp:full_e_hsfp};
bounded proxy (~8–10 rounds); IID; validation only (NO test set). Claude runs these on host GPU
sequentially after Codex returns commands.

## Promotion criterion (declared before running)
Phase-1 proxy PASS if: all four methods run to completion on GPU with finite losses and MONOTONE-ish
increasing validation top-1 (non-trivial > random 1%), a distinct output dir each, and the fair-
comparison matrix confirms a matched partition/seed/metric (or explicitly lists the mismatch +
control). Then define the budget for full B_d reproduction. Do NOT declare B_d from the proxy.

## Rejection/rollback criterion
If methods cannot share one partition/seed/metric, STOP and report the specific incompatibility as a
fairness blocker (do not fabricate a match). If a proxy diverges/NaNs, treat as routine and fix.

