codex
The audit has found a mixed verdict: the six methods can generate the identical IID client partition when launched through `main.py` with the same explicit seed, and every primary score is top-1 accuracy. However, their evaluation schedules/pipelines, training budgets, optimizers, schedulers, and effective architectures are not fully matched; additionally, all CIFAR “validation” objects alias the official test split. I’ll encode those as explicit fairness flags rather than calling the historical defaults fair.
